  "source_caption": "Joseph Gordon-Levitt later said that many viewers misunderstood (500) Days of Summer, noting that Tom isn’t meant to be a romantic hero. The film was intentionally written to show how his idealized view of love blinds him to reality—something that becomes clearer on rewatch.\n\n(500) Days of Summer (2009), directed by Marc Webb, starring Joseph Gordon-Levitt, Zooey Deschanel, Geoffrey Arend. A witty and bittersweet take on modern romance that deconstructs love, expectations, and heartbreak through memory, music, and nonlinear storytelling.\n\n#500DaysOfSummer #JosephGordonLevitt #RomCom #IndieFilm #ModernClassic",
